\solution{Detailed solution -- Exercise 1}
The observed population is the \textbf{210 surveyed customers}; the statistical unit is \textbf{one customer}. The variable is the \textbf{maximum acceptable price}. It is a \textbf{continuous quantitative variable}. Satisfaction (satisfied/not satisfied) is a \textbf{qualitative variable}. A bar chart or pie chart is suitable. A mean and standard deviation are not appropriate for these qualitative categories.

\solution{Detailed solution -- Exercise 2}
\[
N=4+12+32+32+60+35+25+5+5=210.
\]
For each class, $f_i=n_i/210$ and $d_i=n_i/a_i$.
\begin{center}\scriptsize
\begin{tabular}{lrrrrrrrrr}
\toprule
Class&$[10,14[$&$[14,18[$&$[18,26[$&$[26,30[$&$[30,35[$&$[35,40[$&$[40,45[$&$[45,50[$&$[50,55[$\\\midrule
$n_i$&4&12&32&32&60&35&25&5&5\\
$a_i$&4&4&8&4&5&5&5&5&5\\
$f_i$ (\%)&1.90&5.71&15.24&15.24&28.57&16.67&11.90&2.38&2.38\\
$d_i$&1&3&4&8&12&7&5&1&1\\
ICC&4&16&48&80&140&175&200&205&210\\
DCC&210&206&194&162&130&70&35&10&5\\
ICRF (\%)&1.90&7.62&22.86&38.10&66.67&83.33&95.24&97.62&100\\
DCRF (\%)&100&98.10&92.38&77.14&61.90&33.33&16.67&4.76&2.38\\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}\end{center}
Example:
\[
f_{[18,26[}=32/210=15.24\%,\quad ICC_{[26,30[}=4+12+32+32=80.
\]
With unequal class widths, rectangle \emph{area} must represent the count, so height is the density $n_i/a_i$.
\begin{center}\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=.92\linewidth,height=6cm,xlabel={Price (euros)},ylabel={Count density},xmin=10,xmax=55,ymin=0,ymax=13,xtick={10,14,18,26,30,35,40,45,50,55},ymajorgrids]\addplot[ybar interval,fill=gray!45,draw=black] coordinates {(10,1)(14,3)(18,4)(26,8)(30,12)(35,7)(40,5)(45,1)(50,1)(55,1)};\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}\end{center}
\begin{center}\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=.92\linewidth,height=6cm,xlabel={Price (euros)},ylabel={Cumulative count},xmin=10,xmax=55,ymin=0,ymax=220,legend pos=south east,grid=major]\addplot[mark=*] coordinates {(10,0)(14,4)(18,16)(26,48)(30,80)(35,140)(40,175)(45,200)(50,205)(55,210)};\addlegendentry{ICC}\addplot[mark=square*] coordinates {(10,210)(14,206)(18,194)(26,162)(30,130)(35,70)(40,35)(45,10)(50,5)(55,0)};\addlegendentry{DCC}\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}\end{center}
Less than 35 euros: $140/210=66.67\%$. At least 35 euros: $70/210=33.33\%$.

